# Snyk policy file for the cowork repository.
#
# This file lists explicit, justified suppressions for Snyk findings
# that we have reviewed and accepted as architecturally required. Every
# entry MUST include a `reason:` and an `expires:` date so the policy
# is re-reviewed periodically (default cadence: 12 months).
#
# Customer hand-off note: the cowork web Docker image (the artifact the
# customer actually pulls) ships only the compiled `cowork-server` PyPI
# package (installed into /opt/venv) plus the SPA bundle. It does NOT
# contain this repo's `src/main/` Electron sources NOR the local
# `server/` source tree, so Snyk Code findings against either (e.g.
# `oauth-service.ts`, the old `server/routes/*.py` guards) do not appear
# in the customer's Snyk Container scan. There is nothing to suppress for
# the image-only threat model.
#
# The earlier Snyk remediation pass closed every visible High in the
# local Python server (server/main.py, server/routes/*.py) by hardening
# the existing guards rather than suppressing. That source is no longer
# part of the shipped image — it now runs from the published
# cowork-server package — so those fixes are historical from the image's
# point of view. A true scan of the shipped image (OS + the cowork-server
# dependency closure) is 0 HIGH / 0 CRITICAL (Trivy + ECR, 2026-06-09),
# so the `ignore:` map below is empty. Add entries here only when
# refactoring is impractical and the construct is genuinely required.

version: v1.25.0

# See `.trivyignore` (sibling file, repo root) for the equivalent
# Trivy/Aqua CVE allowlist — same rationale per CVE, same review cadence.
# When Snyk Container surfaces one of those CVEs under a Snyk-specific
# rule ID, mirror it here with the matching reason text.

ignore: {}

patch: {}
